codemap 9
tour ui-tree
kind layer
author ai
group render
note The element tree the whole GUI is built from, the ui crate's Ui: no widget objects, no retained state, no framework. Every frame the app opens and closes elements; each is nothing, text, or a custom draw function, and each has a size per axis that is exact, fits its content, or grows into what its parent has left. Nothing is positioned while the tree is being built - layout runs once in end, as recursive passes over the finished tree: each axis gets a fit pass bottom-up and a grow pass top-down, then one pass places everything. Input is answered from the previous frame's rectangles: an element with an id learns whether it is hovered, clicked or dragged one frame late, which is what lets the caller branch on a click in the same statement that creates the element. The crate knows nothing about codemap and nothing about wgpu or winit: fonts reach it as one Measure (cell and row size at a pixel size), and drawing leaves it as a DrawList built through a Canvas (see ui-canvas), which the platform crate's Renderer replays. That boundary is why the whole tree can be built, laid out and drawn in a unit test with a fixed 8x16 cell and no GPU.

