symbol place
lines 0 36
hash bc581329b11aa71d
note Positions, top-down: an element's rectangle comes from the position its parent gave it, its clip is its parent's clip narrowed by the parent's own rectangle when the parent clips, and then it walks a cursor along its own direction placing its children, applying the cross-axis alignment and subtracting the scroll offset. The extent the cursor reached is stored as the content size, which is what the next frame clamps a scroll against. A floating child is placed at its own absolute position and clipped only by the screen.

step 27nlma
order 18
